  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration is config_031 (multimodal, multi-profile, scvi_n200, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.678 acc. The image-only ResNet50 model was very weak (0.208), yet weighted fusion still boosted multimodal performance over RNA-only (0.678 vs 0.650), suggesting the image modality contributes complementary signal but is limited by encoder quality. ViT-L has not yet been tested in any configuration. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to ViT-L improve multimodal performance when all other settings (scvi_n200, multi-profile, avgpool, weighted) are held at their best-known values? Why this is the best next experiment: config_037 is a single-variable change from the current best (config_031), cleanly isolating the effect of image encoder quality. If ViT-L helps, it identifies a promising direction for further exploitation; if it does not, it confirms that the image modality's contribution is bounded regardless of encoder, redirecting effort toward RNA-side improvements. This is more informative than testing aggregation (transformer ≈ avgpool already shown for scvi_n200) or other encoders (scgpt already underperforms)."
}

